"""
Tutorial 2 — Linearization.

Linearizes the open-loop F16 plant about the trim operating point, from the five control
inputs (u1..u5 = T, el, ail, rud, lef; the leading-edge flap is inert in this plant, so its
column of the linearization is zero) to the 12 measured outputs (y1..y12). It reuses the
instrumented design model `LQGDemo` (03_lqg_continuous.dyad) and opens the feedback loop
at the measurement outputs, so the plant keeps its trim command inputs while the
controller feedback is severed — the result is the bare plant P, not the closed loop. The
analysis points `u` and `y` are vector-valued, one channel per element (see the note in 03).

Output: poles, zeros, and Bode/step responses of the linearized plant.
"""
analysis TutorialLinearize
  extends DyadControlSystems.LinearAnalysis(inputs = ["u"], outputs = ["y"], loop_openings = ["y"])
  model = LQGDemo()
relations
end
